Experimental design

1. Sample size
Describe how sample size was determined.

The goal of this study was to survey animal species within the phylum Chordata (vertebrates)
for the purposes of virus discovery. In total, we collected more than 186 host species to
represent as much diversity as possible within the phylum Chordata. For each host species,
1-24 individuals we collected, depending on the availability of animals in the field. Since it is a
discovery study, the number of individuals is irrelevant to the conclusions drawn in the paper.

